WEBVTT

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.500
What's happening?

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:46.280
I am His Imperial Majesty's 
loyal knight, Oslo El Gustave!

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.850
You are all poisonous insects that defile 
His Imperial Majesty's sacred garden.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:57.340
And now the flames of my wrath
 shall immolate you, down to your very souls!

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:00.240
L'age Soleil!

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.360
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.680
Is that what they call
Duke Fastidious' Heaven's Flames?

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.890
<b>It Seems Aoi's Specs Are 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hGreater Than Imagined!</b>

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.760
Tsukasa!

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.030
Wh-What should we be doing?!

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.020
Do you have to ask? 
The fires will reach us here soon!

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.640
We need to escape!

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.480
B-But there are residents who 
haven't escaped yet over there!

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:58.760
Run!

00:02:58.760 --> 00:02:59.740
Run!

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.090
Do not panic!

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:09.750
I am the god of the 
Seven-Light Faith, Akatsuki!

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.450
That's Akatsuki!

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.750
Akatsuki!

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.750
Dormundt has just been subjected to
a cowardly attack from the empire!

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.360
The empire is trying to destroy this city, 
along with its former nobility!

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.310
But fear not!

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.290
We, the Seven-Light Faith, 
will not abandon you!

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.020
Not a single one of you!

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:35.650
That's right! Section 2, Paragraph 3
of the Emergency Manual!

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.990
Looks like you remembered it on your own.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:43.580
We've already notified you of every step
 to be taken when situations like these arise,

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.500
and all the necessary manpower 
and supplies are in place.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.970
All that's left is to remain calm,

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.150
and proceed with your tasks 
steadily and certainly.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:57.450
As the ones who'll lead this city for
 the considerable future, this is <i>your</i> job.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.300
It'll be all right. You can do this.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:05.310
Contact the trading company 
and procure blankets!

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.550
Understood!

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.310
You two transfer our important documents!

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.010
Yes, sir!

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.840
I'll secure our shelter!

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.560
Let's go!

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.560
Yes, sir!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.150
Ohoshi Ringo

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.150
Calling

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:20.670
<i>It's me.</i>

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.520
Tsukasa, are you okay?

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.660
<i>Yeah, everything's fine here.</i>

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.910
Ringo, I'm sorry to keep asking things of you,
 but I'd like to make another request.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.140
Sure, I understand.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.540
Damn it!

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:45.370
What in the world is happening?!

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:47.480
Why is Duke Gustave...?

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.350
W-We imperial nobles are 
still here in the city!

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:03.650
You're...

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.530
Zest Bernard!

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.910
Are you boys all okay?

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:12.330
Why would you rescue us 
after leaving to join the rebel army?!

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.530
For the sake of the kind world to come.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.420
Huh?

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:20.520
Everyone, regardless of status or pedigree,
 will be able to choose how they live...

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.570
And how they die.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.590
That's how the new world will be.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.180
This is no time to be caring about
nobility or whatnot.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.680
What? That's nonsense!

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.120
I'm serious.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.730
That's the world the Seven-Light Faith
is genuinely trying to build.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:53.470
Now I see. You made the streets wider

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:56.010
to prevent fires from 
spreading to other areas.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:56.620
Yeah.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.960
Otherwise, we wouldn't be able to 
extinguish the fires with just water.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.530
Impressive, Tsukasa.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:04.700
Looks like the fire's stopped 
progressing for now.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:11.220
A cunning trick!

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:17.580
Don't think you can escape my wrath so easily!

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:26.940
What's that?

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.330
A-A person just—

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:51.220
This is the true power of my loyalty!

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.010
Die!

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:52.780
Die!

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.620
Die and repent!

00:06:54.620 --> 00:07:00.730
Repent for your sin of trampling down 
His Imperial Majesty's holy land!

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.480
This is bad.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.340
Take all of the wounded and 
evacuate to the central park!

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.870
Hey, if this keeps up...

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.830
I still have one more idea.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:26.550
Everyone!

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:36.490
There's a way to break L'age Soleil!

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:43.230
Unless the lance that serves as the curse core
binding the fire spirits is destroyed,

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.650
L'age Soleil will continue to spread its flames.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.230
But that also means—

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:53.990
If we destroy that lance, 
then we can stop it, right?

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.910
Y-Yes!

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.280
I see.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.200
But how do you know about that, Lyrule?

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:02.570
I don't know.

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:03.670
You don't know?

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.980
I don't know.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.670
I don't know how, but I still know it.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.420
The moment I saw those flames,

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:14.430
the nature of what that was,

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.890
what kind of spell it was...

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:22.180
All of those details just 
naturally popped into my head.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.670
But it's true!

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.890
Unless we destroy the core of that curse,

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:29.020
the flames will continue chasing us forever!

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:30.940
That's how that spell works!

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.690
Please believe me!

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.420
I believe you.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.940
You do believe me?

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:43.710
The changes within you have put you

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:47.400
in a state of such fear and confusion 
that you can't stop shaking,

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:52.580
but you still took action 
to help everyone here.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.340
There's no reason for me 
not to believe in that courage.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.600
<i>Sorry for the wait, bear!</i>

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.760
Ringo, are there any remaining missiles?

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:14.110
J-Just one inside of Bearabbit.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:18.870
Huh? Wait, are you telling me 
this idea you mentioned is...

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.630
Destroying the lance.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:25.140
<i>But we couldn't do any damage to it 
with our ground-to-air missiles, bear.</i>

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.160
Apparently, the strength of a magic spell

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.300
is proportional to the number 
of spirits it commands.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:35.530
For a tactical spell on this scale, 
the concentration of spirits and the strength

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.760
are probably immeasurable.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.820
So it makes sense that we couldn't 
destroy it with our missiles.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.350
However...

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:50.810
The fire spirits bound to L'age Soleil 
are now scattered throughout the city.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.480
We should be able to destroy the lance now.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.480
All right, so...

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.810
But u-um...

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.120
With so much fire burning around it,

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.420
the targeting might fail.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:07.070
<i>The lance is stuck into the ground,</i>

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:09.370
<i>so it's outside the range 
of our anti-air radar, bear.</i>

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:14.340
Then why don't we just have Bearabbit 
make his way directly to the lance?

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.030
<i>I-Impossible!</i>

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:21.350
<i>If I go out into such high heat,
my circuitboards will melt apart, bear!</i>

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:26.460
That makes destroying it 
with a missile difficult.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.370
In that case, I'll go.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.240
What do you mean, you'll go?

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:45.550
I'll run alongside the missile
Bearabbit launches

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:48.500
and manually guide it to its target.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.420
What?!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:53.900
Even knowing you, that's—

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:55.130
Tsukasa-dono.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:59.000
Do you think I'm foolish enough
to take on something I can't achieve

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:03.010
and place everyone else in peril?

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.170
All right. I'll trust you.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:12.020
You are Ichijou Aoi, the super sword master.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:28.340
Ringo! I'm all set now!

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:46.520
<i>All set here, too!</i>

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:54.020
<i>Missile...</i>

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.660
<i>launch, bear!</i>

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.330
Incredible.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:15.470
She really is running alongside that missile.

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:18.090
I'm surprised her legs can keep up with it.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:21.970
At this rate, they should reach 
their destination soon, right?

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:25.470
No, it looks like it won't go that smoothly.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.450
I-Incredible!

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:43.700
This is bad!

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.260
That path's—

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:59.320
Up... you... go!

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.240
She dodged it!

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:06.260
Incredible.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.760
But she can't reach the lance like this.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.280
I can see it over there!

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.540
All right! Just a straight line from here!

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:40.150
Crafty flies!

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:44.760
Go down!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:50.980
Go down, go down, go down, go down!

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:10.410
Where did you hide, you worm?!

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.040
I see it!

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:18.290
Ringo!

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:22.790
Locked on!

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.130
I won't let you!

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:36.810
Art of Void:

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:41.020
Dew Blade Draft!

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:53.370
Go!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.690
Impossible!

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:09.300
This can't be!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:21.180
We did it!

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.210
<i>Hip, hip, hooroar!</i>

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:23.500
Aoi...

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:29.190
Honestly, that girl can be so reckless.

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:34.180
The flames are dying out.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.250
My lord!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.210
Those bastards!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:54.760
Those poisonous bugs devouring 
His Imperial Majesty's sacred garden!

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:13.200
The fire spirits have been 
freed from the curse.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.890
Thank you.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:18.330
Thank you, ladies.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:22.370
They're thanking you all.

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:26.000
You can hear the voices of the spirits?

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.210
Yes.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:33.590
They were in such pain, crying "Help," 
and "We don't want to do this."

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:36.250
But it's fine now.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.520
They won't try to burn the city down.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:39.850
That's good.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.980
Lyrule, allow me to thank you as well.

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:51.690
It was your courage that kept this city
 from facing greater damage.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:53.050
Thank you.

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:04.560
There are a lot of people 
we couldn't save, though...

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:09.740
"This never would have happened 
if we hadn't gone to war."

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:13.070
If that's what you're thinking and 
regretting, then you're wrong.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:13.840
Huh?

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.770
This war...

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:19.720
This whole process of a people's 
revolution against the feudal system

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:23.020
is always guaranteed to happen
at some point in history.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:29.290
Even if Elm Village hadn't started 
this fight for freedom and equality,

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:32.200
eventually someone else would 
have started it elsewhere.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:37.320
After all, there's no future 
for a nation that's willing

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.740
to slaughter its own citizens so mercilessly.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:46.600
What we need to do to make sure none 
of these sacrifices were in vain

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:49.960
is to see this battle through to the end

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.580
and create a future that 
saves thousands more lives.

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:54.630
Don't you agree?

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:57.500
Yes!

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.450
Um, Tsukasa?

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:07.520
I heard a mysterious voice just 
before all of this commotion.

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:12.300
I was suddenly filled with
 all that knowledge about magic,

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.570
and I could hear the spirits' voices.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.400
That timing's all too convenient.

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:19.640
Yes.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:22.580
There's a lot I don't understand, but...

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:27.470
I think "my power" might 
be knowledge of magic

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:30.580
and the power to hear 
the voices of the spirits.

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:36.560
So I'd like to start studying magic!

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:40.590
Once I do, I might be 
able to fight alongside you, too!

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:43.640
If whatever spoke to me

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:47.290
is related to whatever
 brought you all here to this world,

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:51.220
then I might be able to discover a way
to return you all to your world, too!

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:52.420
So...

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:59.030
Yeah, that would be a huge help for us.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:02.840
Akatsuki!

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:07.270
Akatsuki! Thank you for saving us!

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:10.370
That's our Seven-Light Faith!

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.880
<i>No way!</i>

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:15.230
Too loud, Shinobu.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:16.440
<i>I mean, are you serious?</i>

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:18.840
<i>He already sent L'age Soleil your way?!</i>

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:19.630
Yeah.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:21.230
And you're okay?!

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:24.140
I heard that's a really dangerous spell!

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:26.440
Thanks to everyone's efforts,

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:30.330
we were able to limit the damage
to a third of the city.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:33.120
However, it would be difficult 
for us to survive

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:35.020
if he launches it multiple times.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:37.830
<i>You won't have to worry on that front.</i>

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:45.030
He has to spend a fair deal of time 
binding fire spirits to use that tactical spell.

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:48.990
So he shouldn't be able to just pop them out.

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:50.260
<i>I see.</i>

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.420
Still, how humiliating.

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:58.620
I pride myself on exposing all manner of
corruption and scandals before they go public,

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:00.890
but now I was caught unawares!

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:04.440
I can't believe he launched it
 without talking to his forces!

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:08.410
Just how impatient is Gustave?!

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:09.430
I hope he goes bald!

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:13.340
You should stop spouting curses 
like that into your phone.

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:14.940
<i>Come on...</i>

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.440
Well, it's over now.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:20.140
More importantly, this resistance...

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:22.080
You said it was the Azure Brigade?

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.700
You did well to make contact with them.

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.290
Please continue working with them

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:31.900
and feeding me all the strategic 
information they know.

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:34.710
That includes the Azure Brigade's 
inner secrets, too.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:38.410
<i>We haven't yet determined 
if they're fit to ally with.</i>

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:39.420
Yeah.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:42.220
I'll text you what I know so far.

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:43.880
Please do.

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:49.180
Shinobu sounded pretty upset there.

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:52.330
She was lamenting being a step behind.

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:57.770
Thanks to you creating that 
register ahead of time,

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:01.180
it looks like we won't have any 
trouble rebuilding the city.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:02.730
That's good to hear.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.170
Merchant.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:09.360
Apparently, Lyrule heard a voice telling her

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:13.160
to "guide the seven heroes" earlier.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.920
Oh? That's specific.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:18.290
After what happened in Findolf's castle,

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:23.360
I'd kind of seen it coming, but...

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:28.040
At the very least, 
she doesn't seem like an enemy.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:30.180
Though she's not necessarily our ally.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:34.480
Well, now that we've decided to go 
through with this people's revolution,

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:39.190
obtaining information on how to return 
to Earth isn't as high of a priority.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:40.470
Yeah.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:44.730
After this incident, the empire 
is certain to make a move.

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:46.280
What's your plan?

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:47.560
Well...

